<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jayachandra</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1170–<a href="/years/1194">1194</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> · Also known as Jaichand, Jayachchandra, Jayachandra of the Gahadavala dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jayachandra was the last major king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gahadavala-dynasty">Gahadavala dynasty</a>, ruling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varanasi">Varanasi</a> from about 1170 to 1194. He held a large kingdom in the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges plain</a> and was a rival of the Chahamana king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prithviraj-chauhan">Prithviraj Chauhan</a>, a rivalry much elaborated in later bardic legend. He was defeated and killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-of-ghor">Muhammad of Ghor</a> at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-chandawar">Battle of Chandawar</a> in 1194.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jayachandra.jpg" alt="Jayachandra" width="320" height="279" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Utkarsh Nandan Oreya · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Statue_of_King_Jaichand_of_Kannauj,_Raja_Jaichand_Mounds,_Kannauj.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
